# =============================================================================
# ↦ — Flat lista to matrix conversio.
# =============================================================================
#
# What this teaches:
#   • Flat to shaped conversion — a flat `list<T>` converts into a `matrix` when the target type witnesses a literal Figura.
#   • Row-major fill — the flat cells fill the matrix row by row, so the first row takes the first two elements.
#
# Common mistakes:
#   • Mismatching the lista length and the target matrix shape — the element counts must agree.
#
# See also: ↦, lista, matrix, tensor
# =============================================================================


# conversio — flat lista to matrix
#
# WHY: the target matrix type witnesses both element type and register shape, so
# the flat lista fills the cells row-major. The matrix `print` nests one lista
# per row.

main {
    let list<f32> l ← [1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 4.0]
    let matrix<f32, [2, 2]> m ← l ↦ matrix<f32, [2, 2]>
    print m
}
